Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["ARC barrel RICH", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"56cf4608-3dc1-3e43-b4fd-9724a93019dd"],

Cell["Geometry and Optica ray tracing of the ARC barrel RICH, from ARCGeometryData.wl (numbers extracted from the ARC XML and C++ constructor), ARCBarrel.wl (pure Mathematica geometry, no Optica) and ARCBarrelOptica.wl (Optica adapter, here adapted to OpticaEM). The three files are in the project folder src/ (moved there on 2026-11-13): ARCBarrel.wl is loaded by the project loader (LoadRICHCase[\"arc\"], src/LoadProject.wl). Global frame {Z beam, X, Y}: the first axis is the beam axis, as in the LHCb optics (changed on 2026-11-13; it was {X, Y, Z beam}). Units: mm, rad; Optica wavelengths in micrometres. The same geometry is the detector \"ARC barrel\" of optics.nb (detector list src/detectors.wl), whose source chr is the cone of Test 1. Use a fresh kernel (Evaluation > Quit Kernel) if optics.nb was evaluated in the same kernel: the adapter adds its own refractive-index models to ModelRefractiveIndex.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"246e7aca-253e-664d-a4ae-ece6f9c14465"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Geometry (no Optica)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"474d78b5-3c51-3d49-9491-f5f32260d6f3"],

Cell["(*FIX 2026-11-13: the ARC files are in src/; ARCBarrel.wl is loaded by the project loader (case \"arc\" of src/LoadProject.wl)*)\nGet[FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]],\"src\",\"LoadProject.wl\"}]];\nLoadRICHCase[\"arc\"];", "Input",
 CellTags->"FIX-2026-11-13"],

