Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Notes", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b26fc34d-18f9-1843-8bfb-c7ec9ab41ab5"],

Cell["\<\
Whole barrel: ARCOpticaSystem[b1] builds all 17 cells of a row, but \
DrawSystem of the whole barrel is not useful: Optica draws every flat face \
with its 1.2 m \[Times] 1.2 m search rectangle (it hides the rays) and the \
output is about 60 MB. Trace one cell at a time as above, and use \
ARCBarrelGraphics or ARCBarrelSection for the geometry. FullBoundaryModel -> \
False (used here) keeps the inner mirror surface, the aerogel and cooling \
faces and the sensor front; True adds all solid boundary faces.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1ecdbbb4-1543-0c43-9a0d-505cb1b42d74"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
